.\"t
.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 1.18
.\"
.TH "convLogicalTimeToRealTime" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
convLogicalTimeToRealTime \- convert the specified logical time to system time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]stp.convLogicalTimeToRealTime(<logicalTime>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Stp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to convert the specified logical time to system time.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
logicalTime ( \f[I]number, required\f[] )
.PP
Logical time in microseconds.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of type
BSONObj.
Users can get the converted system time through this object.
For field descriptions is as follows:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l l l.
T{
0
T}@T{
Name
T}@T{
Type
T}@T{
Description
T}
_
T{
1
T}@T{
RealTime
T}@T{
timestamp
T}@T{
System time in
T}
T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
microseconds.
T}
.TE
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0.4 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP "1." 3
Get the current logical time.
.nf
\f[C]
> var stp = new Stp()
> stp.getTimeUS()
{
  "TimeStamp": 1679339776883577,
  "TimeError": 1000000
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP "2." 3
Convert logical time to system time.
.nf
\f[C]
> stp.convLogicalTimeToRealTime(1679339776883577)
{
  "RealTime": {
    "$timestamp": "2023\-03\-20\-10.36.16.000582"
  }
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
